Algorithm
Start.
Define the Alpha-Beta function.
If the current node is a leaf node, return its value.
If it is the Maximizer's turn, choose the maximum value and update alpha.
If it is the Minimizer's turn, choose the minimum value and update beta.
If alpha ≥ beta, stop exploring the remaining branches (pruning).
Return the optimal value.
Stop.
Time Complexity
Best Case: O(b^(d/2))
Worst Case: O(b^d)

where:

b = branching factor
d = depth of the game tree
